// Title: Potential Data Exfiltration To Chat Service Webhook Via CommandLine
// Sigma ID: 6293e711-ebf5-4dd8-a1c0-4414679d75a8
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-10-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: exfiltration, T1567.004
// Description: Detects command lines that reference a Discord, Slack or Microsoft Teams incoming webhook URL or
//   the Telegram Bot API, e.g. "curl.exe -F file=@..." or "Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post".
//   Infostealers and adversaries abuse these webhooks as an easy, authenticated-by-URL exfiltration
//   channel to reputable domains that are rarely blocked.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate automation, monitoring or CI/CD scripts that post notifications to Slack, Microsoft Teams, Discord or Telegram channels
// References:
//   - https://discord.com/developers/docs/resources/webhook
//   - https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks
//   - https://core.telegram.org/bots/api
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/388942adbd9641f4dfdcf079d7efe9a75ec0ac43/atomics/T1567.004/T1567.004.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/573709020e1e27abc25818e6f1bb800a6975a121/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_chat_webhook_exfiltration.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "api.telegram.org/bot" or ProcessCommandLine contains "discord.com/api/webhooks/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "discordapp.com/api/webhooks/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "hooks.slack.com/" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".webhook.office.com/"
